theorem.content:
\label{thm:main}
For a skew-symmetrizable matrix $B$, the following are equivalent:
\begin{itemize}
\item[$(1)$] $B$ is of finite type.
\item[$(2)$] The $g$-fan $\mathcal{F}(B)$ is complete, that is, its support $|\mathcal{F}(B)|=\mathbb{R}^n$.
\item[$(3)$] The support $|\mathcal{F}(B)|$ contains all lattice points in $\mathbb{Z}^n$.
\end{itemize}

