\begin{theorem} \label{thm main}
    The totally nonnegative part of the Peterson variety is homeomorphic to the strongly dominant weight polytope as a cell-decomposed space. In particular, it is a regular CW-complex, which is homeomorphic to a cube.
\end{theorem}

